# Git stores LF in every blob, and checks LF out on every platform. Without
# this, core.autocrlf=true turns the working tree back into CRLF on Windows,
# which is what makes `gofmt -l .` flag every file there while it passes on
# Linux and macOS.
#
# An existing Windows checkout keeps its CRLF files until they are rewritten:
#
#   git add --renormalize . && git checkout -- .
#
# A fresh clone gets LF from the start.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is happiest with CRLF in a batch file, and PowerShell's parser is
# unforgiving about a lone LF in some contexts. These two are Windows-only, so
# pinning them costs nothing anywhere else.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
